1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,938
OK, everybody.

2
00:00:03,938 --> 00:00:08,099
I want to welcome Harry and his daughter Michelle

3
00:00:08,099 --> 00:00:09,664
to Thanksgiving with us.

4
00:00:09,664 --> 00:00:11,124
Thank you, Dr. Stewart.

5
00:00:11,124 --> 00:00:12,245
Call me Philip.

6
00:00:12,245 --> 00:00:12,579
OK.

7
00:00:12,579 --> 00:00:15,837
But first, I think we should take a moment

8
00:00:15,837 --> 00:00:18,456
and remember the meaning of Thanksgiving.

9
00:00:18,456 --> 00:00:20,846
Philip, I took Michelle to a school play

10
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:22,179
about the first Thanksgiving.

11
00:00:22,179 --> 00:00:25,324
Well, why don't you tell us about that, Michelle?

12
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:27,071
Thanksgiving was about the Pilgrims,

13
00:00:27,071 --> 00:00:28,417
the first settlers in America.

14
00:00:28,417 --> 00:00:31,220
They shared the first harvest with the Indians

15
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:32,758
and gave thanks.

16
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:33,508
All right.

17
00:00:33,508 --> 00:00:36,767
Then in that spirit let each of us give thanks.

18
00:00:36,767 --> 00:00:38,714
Each in his own way.

19
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:39,714
Who wants to begin?

20
00:00:39,714 --> 00:00:40,381
I will.

21
00:00:40,381 --> 00:00:45,764
I give thanks for being here with my family and for being well,

22
00:00:45,764 --> 00:00:47,980
so I can enjoy you all.

23
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:48,647
All rihgt!

24
00:00:48,647 --> 00:00:50,625
We love you, Grandpa.

25
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:59,559
I'd like to give thanks for a healthy year, a good job,

26
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:02,833
and for meeting Harry and Michelle.

27
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:05,201
We'd like to give thanks for meeting Susan

28
00:01:05,201 --> 00:01:07,015
and the Stewart family.

29
00:01:07,015 --> 00:01:09,528
I love you, Daddy.

30
00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:10,218
Thanks, Harry.

31
00:01:10,218 --> 00:01:11,949
That was very kind of you.

32
00:01:11,949 --> 00:01:14,449
I'd like to give thanks for Grandpa coming to live with us.

33
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,498
And I'd also like to thank my math teacher

34
00:01:16,498 --> 00:01:20,405
for giving me a passing grade.

35
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:24,050
And call me, Alexandra.

36
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:26,361
Oh, Robbie!

37
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:27,121
She'll call.

38
00:01:27,121 --> 00:01:28,641
You go first, Marilyn.

39
00:01:28,641 --> 00:01:29,339
I'm thinking.

40
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,317
You go first.

41
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:35,295
Well, you all know I'm working on my photo album.

42
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:38,273
It's not finished yet.

43
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:41,251
And I'd like to thank Marilyn for being so patient.

44
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:44,229
Thanks, Richard.

45
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,780
I should thank you for encouraging me

46
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:47,527
to keep working on my fashion designs.

47
00:01:47,527 --> 00:01:53,163
I'm lucky to have a husband with an artistic eye.

48
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:58,140
Oh, we have a lot to be thankful for.

49
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,404
For the food on this table.

50
00:02:00,404 --> 00:02:02,096
Just like the Pilgrims.

51
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:04,256
I'll go along with that, Ellen.

52
00:02:04,256 --> 00:02:08,052
Well, help me serve, Robbie.

53
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:11,255
It was a wonderful meal, Mrs. Stewart.

54
00:02:11,255 --> 00:02:11,704
Thank you.

55
00:02:11,704 --> 00:02:14,008
And now to see the end of the football game.

56
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:14,488
Exactly.

57
00:02:14,488 --> 00:02:16,986
Where are you going, Philip?

58
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:19,419
Remember, the Michigan football game?

59
00:02:19,419 --> 00:02:22,942
And Michigan needs a touchdown.

60
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,342
Did you forget something?

61
00:02:25,342 --> 00:02:27,451
Dad, your famous apple pie.

62
00:02:27,451 --> 00:02:29,755
Just let me see the score, Ellen.

63
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:30,398
Go ahead, Philip.

64
00:02:30,398 --> 00:02:33,296
We should all take a little break before dessert.

65
00:02:33,296 --> 00:02:44,892
Oh, who could that be?

66
00:02:44,892 --> 00:02:47,623
Oh, it must be Alexandra.

67
00:02:47,623 --> 00:02:50,944
I invited her to come by for dessert.

68
00:02:50,944 --> 00:02:52,722
You did?

69
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:53,922
I like Ellen.

70
00:02:53,922 --> 00:02:55,010
You know everyone, Alexandra.

71
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:58,189
No, she doesn't know Harry Bennett and his daughter Michelle.

72
00:02:58,189 --> 00:02:59,878
Nice to meet you.

73
00:02:59,878 --> 00:03:00,278
Hi.

74
00:03:00,278 --> 00:03:02,149
Hello, Alexandra.

75
00:03:02,149 --> 00:03:03,136
Hi, Marilyn.

76
00:03:03,136 --> 00:03:04,123
Hi, Susan.

77
00:03:04,123 --> 00:03:05,244
Happy Thanksgiving.

78
00:03:05,244 --> 00:03:07,612
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

79
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:10,589
Please sit down, Alexandra.

80
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
Dad, Richard--Alexandra's here.

81
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:15,567
Michigan needs a touchdown.

82
00:03:15,567 --> 00:03:17,402
Three minutes to play.

83
00:03:17,402 --> 00:03:18,688
Hi, Alexandra. Welcome.

84
00:03:18,688 --> 00:03:19,523
Hello, Alexandra.

85
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:21,957
Yes, Michigan needs a touchdown.

86
00:03:21,957 --> 00:03:25,879
One tiny little touchdown, with just three minutes to play.

87
00:03:25,879 --> 00:03:27,746
You want Michigan to win.

88
00:03:27,746 --> 00:03:28,457
How'd you guess?

89
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:40,369
And Alexandra brought us a pumpkin pie.

90
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:43,347
What happened?

91
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:46,325
We forgot to turn the oven on.

92
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:50,033
We did?

93
00:03:50,033 --> 00:03:52,955
Philip, why don't you go

94
00:03:52,955 --> 00:03:54,752
watch the last three minutes of the game.

95
00:03:54,752 --> 00:03:58,237
I will serve coffee and pumpkin pie.

96
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:01,215
OK. I'll be back in a few minutes.

97
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:04,468
Robbie, would you bring the dessert plates.

98
00:04:04,468 --> 00:04:10,149
And, Marilyn, would you pour coffee, please.

99
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:11,122
Sure, Ellen.

100
00:04:11,122 --> 00:04:14,780
How was your Thanksgiving dinner, Alexandra?

101
00:04:14,780 --> 00:04:16,105
Just wonderful, Mr. Stewart.

102
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:17,556
The Molinas are a large family.

103
00:04:17,556 --> 00:04:19,083
I love being with them.

104
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:20,803
I'm glad you came by, Alexandra.

105
00:04:20,803 --> 00:04:26,338
I am, too.

106
00:04:26,338 --> 00:04:32,310
Touchdown! Touchdown! Touchdown!

107
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:32,967
Great Thanksgiving.

108
00:04:32,967 --> 00:04:34,892
Lots to be thankful for.

109
00:04:34,892 --> 00:04:37,450
Michigan scored a touchdown.

110
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:39,928
Alexandra came by.

111
00:04:39,928 --> 00:04:42,906
And nobody misses Philip's famous apple pie.

112
00:04:42,906 --> 00:04:44,906
Oh, Grandpa!
